  "title": "Alpha power indexes working memory load for durations",
  "description": "Raw magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings from 23 healthy adults performing an n-item delayed temporal reproduction task. Participants held sequences of one or three empty auditory intervals in memory and then reproduced them by button press. The dataset also includes EOG, ECG, digitized head and electrode positions, a two-minute eyes-open resting-state recording, and individual anatomical MRI. It supports research on working memory dynamics, auditory processing, motor responses and resting activity.",
  "methods_description": "MEG was recorded in a magnetically shielded room with a 306-channel Elekta Neuromag Vector View system, sampled at 1 kHz with 0.03-330 Hz online filtering, across 8 task runs of about 10 min each. Head position was measured with HPI coils before each run, and EEG electrode, HPI and fiducial positions were digitized with a Polhemus system. EOG and ECG were recorded, and a resting-state recording followed the task. Individual T1 anatomical MRI was acquired on a Siemens 3T Prisma Fit scanner (1 mm slices, TR 2300 ms, TE 2.98 ms, flip angle 9°). Data were converted to BIDS with MNE-BIDS.",
